<description>The remote finger service accepts redirect requests.  That is, users can perform requests like :

		finger user@host@victim

This allows an attacker to use this computer as a relay to gather information on a third-party network.  In addition, this type of syntax can be used to create a denial of service condition on the remote host.</description>
<epss_score>0.0008</epss_score>
<exploit_code_maturity>Unproven</exploit_code_maturity>
