<script_version>1.15</script_version>
<solution>n/a</solution>
<synopsis>Some information about the remote HTTP configuration can be extracted.</synopsis>
<plugin_output>
Response Code : HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request

Protocol version : HTTP/1.1
HTTP/2 TLS Support: No
HTTP/2 Cleartext Support: No
SSL : no
Keep-Alive : no
Headers :

  Date: Wed, 10 Sep 2025 03:41:19 GMT
  Server: Apache/2.4.58 (Win64) OpenSSL/3.1.3 PHP/8.2.12
  Content-Length: 468
  Connection: close
  Content-Type: text/html; charset=iso-8859-1
  
Response Body :

&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//IETF//DTD HTML 2.0//EN&quot;&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;
&lt;title&gt;400 Bad Request&lt;/title&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Bad Request&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your browser sent a request that this server could not understand.&lt;br /&gt;
Reason: You&apos;re speaking plain HTTP to an SSL-enabled server port.&lt;br /&gt;
 Instead use the HTTPS scheme to access this URL, please.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;address&gt;Apache/2.4.58 (Win64) OpenSSL/3.1.3 PHP/8.2.12 Server at www.example.com Port 443&lt;/address&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;
</plugin_output>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="443" svc_name="www" protocol="tcp" severity="0" pluginID="15588" pluginName="Web Server SSL Port HTTP Traffic Detection" pluginFamily="Web Servers">
<cpe>cpe:/a:apache:http_server</cpe>
<description>Nessus has discovered that it is talking in plain HTTP on an SSL port. 

Nessus has corrected this issue by enabling HTTPS for this port only. However, if other SSL ports are used on the remote host, they might be skipped.</description>
<fname>apache_SSL_complain.nasl</fname>
<plugin_modification_date>2022/04/11</plugin_modification_date>
<plugin_name>Web Server SSL Port HTTP Traffic Detection</plugin_name>
<plugin_publication_date>2004/11/01</plugin_publication_date>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>None</risk_factor>
<script_version>1.23</script_version>
<solution>Enable SSL tests in the &apos;Services&apos; preference setting, or increase the timeouts if this option is already set and the plugin missed this port.</solution>
<synopsis>An SSL detection issue might impede the Nessus Scan.</synopsis>
<thorough_tests>true</thorough_tests>
</ReportItem>
