<description>Nessus was able to run &apos;netstat&apos; on the remote host to enumerate the open ports. If &apos;netstat&apos; is not available, the plugin will attempt to use &apos;ss&apos;.

See the section &apos;plugins options&apos; about configuring this plugin.

Note: This plugin will run on Windows (using netstat.exe) in the event that the target being scanned is localhost.</description>
<fname>netstat_portscan.nasl</fname>
<plugin_modification_date>2025/05/27</plugin_modification_date>
<plugin_name>Netstat Portscanner (SSH)</plugin_name>
<plugin_publication_date>2004/08/15</plugin_publication_date>
<plugin_type>local</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>None</risk_factor>
<script_version>1.110</script_version>
<see_also>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Netstat</see_also>
<solution>n/a</solution>
<synopsis>Remote open ports can be enumerated via SSH.</synopsis>
<plugin_output>Port 57180/udp was found to be open</plugin_output>
</ReportItem>
